      "notes": "Maine GeoLibrary statewide organized-towns parcel service. Layer 10 carries polygon geometry with COUNTY, TOWN, and location fields. Layer 9 is the assessor attribute table (no geometry) with OWNER1/OWNER2 and mailing address. Join it to layer 10 on STATE_ID, or on GEOCODE plus MAP_BK_LOT; MAP_BK_LOT alone matches other towns' parcels. Filter Cumberland County with COUNTY='CUMBERLAND'; includes Portland, South Portland, Westbrook, Scarborough, Gorham, Windham, etc. Note: submissions are voluntary from municipalities and some towns may have stale data (updated irregularly). Unorganized territories use a separate service (gis.maine.gov/mapservices). Partial coverage, read 2026-11-23: the Census Bureau's TIGERweb list names 28 towns and cities in Cumberland County, and 20 of them have parcels on layer 10 whose STATE_ID joins an assessor row with an owner on layer 9. Covered: Bridgton, Brunswick, Cape Elizabeth, Casco, Cumberland, Falmouth, Gray, Harpswell, Naples, New Gloucester, North Yarmouth, Portland, Pownal, Raymond, Scarborough, Sebago, Standish, Westbrook, Windham and Yarmouth. Not covered: Freeport and South Portland have parcels and assessor rows with owners, but no parcel joins one: their assessor rows write MAP_BK_LOT, and so STATE_ID, in another format than their parcels, and none of Freeport's 4,356 parcels or South Portland's 8,822 matches a row on either key (read 2026-11-23). Search their owners by name on layer 9. Baldwin and Harrison have parcels but no assessor rows, so no owner. Gorham and Long Island have parcels and assessor rows, but every owner in those rows is blank, so no owner. Chebeague Island and Frye Island have no parcels in the service. A blank owner is stored as an empty string, not null, so count owners with CHAR_LENGTH(TRIM(BOTH ' ' FROM OWNER1)) > 0, not IS NOT NULL.",
