      "notes": "York County is Maine's southernmost county and its most densely populated outside the Portland area, with seasonal coastal communities driving heavy property-lookup demand. The data comes from the same Maine GeoLibrary statewide organized-towns service used by Cumberland County. Layer 10 (FeatureServer/10) carries polygon geometry with COUNTY, TOWN, PROP_LOC, MAP_BK_LOT, and STATE_ID. Layer 9 (FeatureServer/9) is the assessor attribute table, with no geometry, carrying OWNER1/OWNER2 and mailing address fields. Join it to layer 10 on STATE_ID, or on GEOCODE plus MAP_BK_LOT; MAP_BK_LOT alone matches other towns' parcels. Filter to York County with COUNTY='YORK'; municipalities include Biddeford, Saco, Sanford, Kennebunk, York, Kittery, Wells, and Berwick. Important caveat: GeoLibrary submissions are voluntary and asynchronous: some towns update quarterly, others lag by a year or more. For current ownership or assessment, check the individual town assessor's office or the Maine Revenue Services PAS database. Unorganized territories in York County use a separate MEGIS service. Partial coverage, read 2026-11-23: the Census Bureau's TIGERweb list names 29 towns and cities in York County, and 14 of them have parcels on layer 10 whose STATE_ID joins an assessor row with an owner on layer 9. Covered: Arundel, Biddeford, Buxton, Dayton, Eliot, Kennebunkport, Lebanon, Limington, Lyman, Ogunquit, Old Orchard Beach, Saco, Sanford and South Berwick. Not covered: Kennebunk and Acton have parcels and assessor rows with owners, but their parcels' STATE_ID does not match their rows' (read 2026-11-23). Kennebunk's parcels write '-' where its assessor rows write '_': read each '-' as '_' and 5,634 of its 7,183 parcels join. Acton's parcels carry a doubled STATE_ID, so only 2 of its 3,056 join on it: join Acton on GEOCODE plus MAP_BK_LOT instead, where 2,992 parcels match exactly one assessor row. Berwick, Kittery, Limerick, Shapleigh, Wells and York have parcels but no assessor rows, so no owner. Hollis and North Berwick have parcels and assessor rows, but every owner in those rows is blank, so no owner. Cornish, Newfield, Parsonsfield and Waterboro have no parcels in the service. Alfred gets no owner here either: layer 10 codes Alfred's parcels GEOCODE 31030, the code of Arundel's parcels and assessor rows, while Alfred's own assessor rows (1,671, every one with an owner) sit under GEOCODE 31020, which this record's layer 9 scope leaves out. Those rows match Alfred's parcels (TOWN = 'Alfred') on MAP_BK_LOT: 1,596 of its 1,634 parcels match exactly one row, and no row's MAP_BK_LOT repeats (read 2026-11-23). A blank owner is stored as an empty string, not null, so count owners with CHAR_LENGTH(TRIM(BOTH ' ' FROM OWNER1)) > 0, not IS NOT NULL.",
